        "title": {
          "en": "Microsoft Research Unveils ADeLe for AI Performance Prediction and Explanation",
          "zh": "微软研究院推出 ADeLe，旨在预测并解释 AI 性能"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "Microsoft researchers, in collaboration with Princeton University and Universitat Politècnica de València, introduced ADeLe to predict and explain AI performance across tasks, aiming to provide insight beyond traditional benchmarks.",
          "zh": "微软研究人员与普林斯顿大学和瓦伦西亚理工大学合作，推出了 ADeLe，旨在预测和解释 AI 在各项任务中的性能，以弥补传统 AI 基准测试的不足。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "ADeLe was developed by Microsoft researchers in collaboration with Princeton University and Universitat Politècnica de València.",
            "Its primary function is to predict and explain AI performance across various tasks.",
            "ADeLe addresses current AI benchmark limitations, which report LLM performance but lack insight into underlying capabilities, failure explanations, or reliable predictions for new tasks."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "ADeLe 由微软研究人员与普林斯顿大学和瓦伦西亚理工大学合作开发。",
            "其主要功能是预测和解释 AI 在不同任务中的性能。",
            "ADeLe 旨在解决现有 AI 基准测试的局限性，即这些测试仅报告大型语言模型 (LLM) 在特定任务上的表现，但未能深入揭示其潜在能力、解释失败原因或可靠预测新任务的结果。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "This development offers a method to move beyond simple performance metrics by explaining AI failures and predicting outcomes on new tasks. It could lead to a more nuanced understanding of AI model capabilities, facilitating targeted improvements and more reliable deployment.",
          "zh": "这一进展提供了一种超越简单性能指标的方法，能够解释 AI 失败原因并预测新任务的结果。这可能促使对 AI 模型能力产生更细致的理解，从而促进有针对性的改进和更可靠的部署。"
        },
        "source": "Microsoft Research",
        "link": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/adele-predicting-and-explaining-ai-performance-across-tasks/"
